a birthday party ended in a shooting  early sunday morning five people injured  and sent to the hospital it happened at  a home on holt avenue near lake mead  boulevard in nellis 8 news now reporter  ryan matthey spoke to the people living  there and neighbors on what they  witnessed  a birthday celebration ends in gunfire  my wife checking the  window i checked outside they look at  the police metro police surrounding this  northeast valley home overnight sunday  five people were shot neighbors say a  fight at the gathering escalated into a  shooting i saw about 10 police cars  lined up  on this street here  i'd never seen that before so i knew  something had happened calvin border and  other neighbors were awakened by the  police presence a source with metro  confirming to 8 news now about a hundred  people were in the backyard when i asked  the residents for an explanation of the  shooting they declined to answer my  questions they actually said they were  unaware of the shooting until they saw  it the next morning on the news they  call this an isolated incident the  surrounding neighbors say otherwise and  they have this house party once or twice  a month  on saturday nights it's pretty you know  pretty often you don't have concerns  that this would happen again i really  don't know what's what's gonna i i  imagine they might put a restriction on  the parties there  from now on that's just my guess  but you know it's uh  things get wild on saturday night  ryan matthew 8 news now  one person is in custody he's been  identified as 36-year-old alberto santa  cruz police would not comment on the  status of each victim and the  circumstances leading to the gunfire
 

